{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>This is the Torah of jealousies.</b> Jealousy enacted with justification and jealousy enacted without justification. He explains this by saying <b>when a woman goes astray under her husband and defiles herself</b> — and this is jealousy with justification." "And he adds and says <b>or a man over whom a spirit of jealousy passes.</b> And this is without cause worthy of it."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The verse quoted (Numbers 5:29) uses תחת אישה, not תחת אישה; I retain Sforno's Hebrew quoting the verse as lemma. His lemma appears to read תשׂטה (from שׂוטה, stray) for MT תִּשְׂטְאֶה."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:48.917666735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}